      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بتّتهُ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَبْتِيتٌ</span>, <i>He cut it off,</i> or <i>severed
it, [entirely,</i> or <i>utterly, and] much,</i> or <i>with extraordinary energy</i> or <i>effectiveness;</i> the teshdeed
denoting intensiveness of signification. (S.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَتَّتُوهُ</span> <i>They furnished him with</i> [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَتَات</span>, or] <i>travel-ling-provisions.</i> (M, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَتِّتْهُمْ</span> <i>Give thou to
them [garments called</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُتُوت</span> [pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَتُّ</span>, q. v.].
(TA, from a trad.)

